## Advanced Synchronization Logic

### Selective Merge (Skip Existing)
Copies all files from source to destination while skipping files that already exist.
```bash
rsync -av --ignore-existing --update --progress /source/dir/ dest_dir/
```
* `--ignore-existing`: Do not update files that already exist in the destination.
* `--update` (`-u`): Copy a file only if the source file is newer than the destination’s.

### Merge Based on Size Only
Copies files while removing them from the source, using file size differences as the only check:
```bash
rsync -a --remove-source-files --progress --size-only source_dir/ dest_dir/
```

### Exact Mirror (Delete Extraneous)
Creates an exact mirror of the source by deleting files in the destination that no longer exist in the source:
```bash
rsync -av --delete source_dir/ dest_dir/
```

