## Option Reference Table

| Option | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `-a` | **Archive mode**: recursive, preserves symlinks, perms, times, group, owner |
| `-v` | **Verbose**: provides details on files being transferred |
| `-z` | **Compress**: reduces data sent over the network |
| `-n` | **Dry Run**: shows what would happen without making changes |
| `-u` | **Update**: skips files that are newer on the destination |
| `-l` | **Links**: preserves symbolic links |
| `-A` / `-X` | Preserve ACLs and Extended Attributes |
| `--delete` | Delete files in destination that aren't in source |
| `--progress` | Show progress bar during transfer |
| `--size-only` | Skip files that match in size (ignore timestamps) |
| `--bwlimit` | Limit I/O bandwidth; KBytes per second |

---

## Update Logic Comparison

| Feature | `--update` (`-u`) | `--ignore-existing` | `--ignore-times` |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Overwrites existing?** | Only if Source is newer | Never | Always |
| **Logic** | Time-based comparison | Existence-based | Content-based (Checksum) |
| **Best Use-case** | Syncing work between devices | Resuming a massive file transfer | When timestamps are broken/unreliable |

